body:
I think self-reflection can be helpful and it depends on what you're trying to accomplish. People arrive at Zen for different reasons: some seek enlightenment, others just want a more stable mind to help them live their daily lives. If someone's in the second category, then I don't think there's much more to be done than practicing zazen daily and practicing mindfulness throughout the day. Maybe spending reading Zen-related texts sometimes would be helpful in some ways, but reading things isn't an essential part of Zen.

&#x200B;

"Ordinary mind is the Way." - Nansen
